            "review_title": "Review at Cham Charm",
            "review_text": "Martin C\nThornbury, Australia51 contributions\n0\nExcellent 5 star buffet in a delightful setting. Visited twice!\nFeb 2018 • Family\nFirst up, let me say that I’m astounded by the negative reviews of Cham Charm that I’ve read. We found the quality of the food, breadth of dishes and the service, to be nothing short of 1st class. \n\nMy Vietnamese wife found Cham Charm online. I’ve been to Vietnam many times but hadn’t heard of it. It was half price during the week, provided we pre-booked. We paid 600,000 DONG per head (~AUD30) which included free -flowing wine. You’d pay 4 times that in Australia and probably significantly more. Moreover, you wouldn’t experience such a great ambience. The setting is really different and perhaps unique: subtle lighting, Champa decor, cascading water, cathedral ceilings, prolific use of stone and ceramics, open spaces as well as nooks and vistas, plenty of room between tables. This made large spaces seem intimate. \n\nWe took my wife’s mother, brother and his girlfriend out for the night. Despite its being advertised as a 5 star seafood buffet (and it is) it has a huge variety of dishes - beef, chicken, curries, casseroles, vegetables and many more. My guess is that there’d be 100 dishes or more, deposited on galleries that were tucked around corners, like hidden vistas. Just when you’d thought you’d seen everything, you’d find another gallery with 20 more dishes. A delicious assortment of deserts was also provided however by the time you discover that you cannot possibly eat anymore oysters, prawns, meat, casseroles or sushi and that much to your disappointment, you’ve only sampled 5% of the fare, there’s not much room left for desert, even if it’s wafer-thin!\n\nThe service was outstanding and as soon as we raised a “yo!” our glasses were immediately topped up by our attentive waiters. We had a waiter hovering, just far enough away, who cleared our places as required. In fact, I now recall we had 2 waiters! \n\nWe had such a lovely evening that on the night before our departure back to Australia, some 4 days later, we took our family and a couple of others back to Cham Charm! Our second visit was as consistent with its excellence as our first. \n\nA stroll along the Bridge of Stars, just outside Cham Charm’s door around the lake with its community of young lovers, topped off both great nights. I guarantee we’ll return on our next visit. \n\nDistrict 7 and Cham Charm are highly recommended!\nRead more\nWritten March 9, 2018",
