            "review_text": "heyphi\nLondon1 contribution\n0\nFalse advertising\nApr 2016 • Couples\nSave your money and pay the little extra to eat the Seafood Buffet at Hotel Nikko. The promotion price was not honoured despite being told it would be by two members of staff, we were rushed from the door to our seats after returning from some shopping. The food is typical of what you would find in a 3* hotel buffet with the exception that lobster is on the menu. Even then the unlimited wine and lobster is not as advertised and restricted, unlike the buffet at Hotel Nikko. When the bill came, the two members of staff were nowhere to be seen so we had to pay full price because apparently we didn't reserve a table and this was a mistake on the restaurants part which they failed to rectify. At full price it's only slightly cheaper than Hotel Nikko and the food was inferior in every way. It was such a horrendous experience settling the bill, I agreed to pay but since they had cheated me of my money, I would be writing this review and telling others of their false advertising. \n\nAvoid this place. Pay the extra and go to Hotel Nikko.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten April 24, 2016",
